The $login variable is built in the PHP files and passed to the Smarty template engine. Here's where it happens:

In the template files, $login appears on these lines:

LEAF_Nexus/templates/main.tpl (line 87): {$login|sanitize}
LEAF_Request_Portal/templates/main.tpl (line 107): {$login}
LEAF_Nexus/admin/templates/main.tpl (line 77): {$login}
In the PHP code that assigns it, look at these files:

LEAF_Nexus/index.php (around line 643):

PHP
$main->assign('login', $t_login->fetch('login.tpl'));
LEAF_Request_Portal/report.php (around line 146):

PHP
$main->assign('login', $t_login->fetch('login.tpl'));
LEAF_Request_Portal/ajaxIndex.php (around line 436):

PHP
$main->assign('login', $t_login->fetch('login.tpl'));
So the $login variable is actually the output of rendering the login.tpl template (a separate Smarty template file), which is then assigned to the main template. The actual login information is formatted in that login.tpl file rather than in main.tpl directly.

